  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Noah … took of every clean beast, and of every clean fowl, Gen. 8:20. that ye may put difference between … unclean and clean, Lev. 10:10. may be clean from all your sins before the Lord, Lev. 16:30. dipped himself seven times in Jordan, … and he was clean, 2 Kgs. 5:14. he that hath clean hands shall be stronger, Job 17:9. He that hath clean hands, and a pure heart, Ps. 24:4. Create in me a clean heart, Ps. 51:10. the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes, Prov. 16:2. Who can say, I have made my heart clean, Prov. 20:9. Wash you, make you clean, Isa. 1:16. be ye clean, that bear the vessels of the Lord, Isa. 52:11 (3 Ne. 20:41; D&C 38:42; 133:5). O Jerusalem! wilt thou not be made clean, Jer. 13:27.",
